to the next question.

253
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:29,267
The question is...

254
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:32,233
"Who founded the Tagalog
newspaper

255
00:13:32,367 --> 00:13:36,667
considered the first nationalist
newspaper in the Philippines?"

256
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:38,000
Emilio Jacinto.

257
00:13:39,500 --> 00:13:41,967
Wrong. Marcelo H. del Pilar.

258
00:13:42,100 --> 00:13:45,367
Emilio Jacinto wrote
the Kartilya ng Katipunan.

259
00:13:45,500 --> 00:13:47,467
It's Emilio Jacinto.

260
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:49,167
Why do you always think
you're right?

261
00:13:52,033 --> 00:13:53,667
Let's go with Marcelo.

262
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:55,333
Trust me.

263
00:13:59,267 --> 00:14:01,633
If we lose this...

264
00:14:01,767 --> 00:14:02,800
this is on you.

265
00:14:02,933 --> 00:14:12,900
[GRIPPING MUSIC]

266
00:14:16,167 --> 00:14:18,133
And the correct answer is...

267
00:14:18,267 --> 00:14:22,567
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC]

268
00:14:22,700 --> 00:14:24,633
"Marcelo H. del Pilar."

269
00:14:24,767 --> 00:14:28,267
Congratulations to our leading
team, Brighton Bay Academy.

270
00:14:29,367 --> 00:14:30,600
You're moving on
to the next round.

271
00:14:30,733 --> 00:14:36,900
["YOU'RE MY FAVORITE SONG"
INSTRUMENTAL]

272
00:14:37,033 --> 00:14:39,267
Go, Angel!

273
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:43,067
I'm sure Calix is the one
carrying their team.

274
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:44,500
Go, Calix!

275
00:14:48,633 --> 00:14:50,133
Go, Calix!

276
00:15:14,733 --> 00:15:15,700
Bebe, what's wrong?

277
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:19,867
I think I recognize one
of those boys.

278
00:15:21,767 --> 00:15:23,333
Those guys?

279
00:15:23,467 --> 00:15:25,333
I think I know them.

280
00:15:25,467 --> 00:15:26,833
They're the ones who are always
playing Mobile Legends

281
00:15:26,967 --> 00:15:29,300
and buying soft drinks here.

282
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:32,967
Kaila, do you know
where I can find them?

283
00:15:33,100 --> 00:15:37,233
I need to know why they trashed
our resort

284
00:15:37,400 --> 00:15:39,733
and whether someone ordered them
to do it.

285
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:43,567
They hang out
at the milk tea shop.

286
00:15:43,700 --> 00:15:45,800
The one called Boba Ka Tea.

287
00:15:45,933 --> 00:15:47,633
- [QUIRKY MUSIC]
- Hey, come on.

288
00:15:47,767 --> 00:15:51,667
Don't call Bebe stupid.

289
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:53,933
No.

290
00:15:54,067 --> 00:15:57,567
Boba Ka Tea is the name
of the milk tea shop.

291
00:15:57,700 --> 00:15:59,467
That's where you should
wait for them, Bebe.

292
00:16:01,633 --> 00:16:02,767
Okay.

293
00:16:09,500 --> 00:16:12,000
And the QuizCon continues!

294
00:16:12,133 --> 00:16:13,433
[PEOPLE CHEERING AND APPLAUDING]

295
00:16:13,567 --> 00:16:16,800
Students, make some noise
for your favorite school!

296
00:16:17,067 --> 00:16:18,767
Brighton Bay!

297
00:16:18,900 --> 00:16:20,800
[PEOPLE WHOOPING]

298
00:16:20,933 --> 00:16:22,433
Let's go, Angel!

299
00:16:23,600 --> 00:16:25,200
Just after two rounds,

300
00:16:25,333 --> 00:16:28,867
we are left with three teams
for the final round,

301
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,267
namely Brighton Bay.

302
00:16:31,400 --> 00:16:34,033
- I want to hear you!
- [PEOPLE CHEERING]

303
00:16:34,167 --> 00:16:35,867
- Calix, go!
- Go, Angel!

304
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:37,500
Go, Brighton!

305
00:16:40,733 --> 00:16:44,167
I want to hear Pacific High!

306
00:16:45,233 --> 00:16:46,967
[PEOPLE CHEERING]

307
00:16:47,100 --> 00:16:49,000
Where's Holy Crest?

308
00:16:49,133 --> 00:16:51,867
[CHEERING]

309
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:54,500
And now it's time for the sink
or swim challenge.

310
00:16:54,633 --> 00:16:58,133
Let's put those physics skills
to the ultimate test.

311
00:16:58,267 --> 00:17:01,000
In this special round,
in just one hour,

312
00:17:01,133 --> 00:17:04,967
you must build a boat using only
cardboard and duct tape.

313
00:17:05,100 --> 00:17:07,500
Using everything you've learned
in physics,

314
00:17:07,633 --> 00:17:09,200
your boat must stay afloat

315
00:17:09,333 --> 00:17:11,933
and make it to the end
of the swimming pool.

316
00:17:12,067 --> 00:17:13,367
Wait, Calix.

317
00:17:13,500 --> 00:17:15,533
The stability is off.

318
00:17:15,700 --> 00:17:16,767
It'll be unstable.

319
00:17:16,900 --> 00:17:18,633
One small movement
and we'll tip over.

320
00:17:19,733 --> 00:17:21,400
Can you stop, Angel?

321
00:17:21,533 --> 00:17:23,367
Stay in your lane.

322
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:25,033
You think you know everything.

323
00:17:27,567 --> 00:17:29,233
You don't.

324
00:17:29,367 --> 00:17:31,933
I know what I'm doing
because I'm better than you.

325
00:17:38,900 --> 00:17:40,933
Calix, we're not competing
against each other.

326
00:17:41,067 --> 00:17:42,800
We're partners here.

327
00:17:42,933 --> 00:17:46,933
What good is speed if we sink
before we're even halfway there?

328
00:17:47,067 --> 00:17:48,433
Calix, are you even listening?

329
00:17:48,600 --> 00:17:49,600
Can you stop, Angel?

330
00:17:50,967 --> 00:17:51,933
You keep talking,

331
00:17:52,067 --> 00:17:53,867
calculating all these variables,

332
00:17:55,733 --> 00:17:57,233
but we're running out of time.

333
00:17:58,933 --> 00:18:01,067
You took charge
in the previous rounds.

334
00:18:02,400 --> 00:18:03,700
This is my round now.

335
00:18:03,833 --> 00:18:07,333
[TENSE MUSIC]

336
00:18:07,467 --> 00:18:08,700
Just get in the boat later.

337
00:18:22,533 --> 00:18:23,800
My god, I can't hear them,

338
00:18:23,933 --> 00:18:25,367
but it looks like they're
arguing.

339
00:18:26,400 --> 00:18:29,767
Holy shoot. Why can't Angel just
let Calix do his thing?

340
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:32,367
Calix is better than her anyway.

341
00:18:36,733 --> 00:18:38,567
Angel, you can do it!

342
00:18:38,700 --> 00:18:40,700
You have to win this
for your grandfather.

343
00:18:44,133 --> 00:18:45,467
- Go, go, go...
- Go, Angel!

344
00:18:45,600 --> 00:18:47,967
- Go, Calix!
- Go, Calix!

345
00:18:48,100 --> 00:18:49,000
Go, go, go...

346
00:18:49,133 --> 00:18:51,500
- Go, Angel!
- Calix, let's go!

347
00:18:51,633 --> 00:18:52,833
Go, Brighton!

348
00:18:54,300 --> 00:18:56,467
Students, on your marks...

349
00:18:58,233 --> 00:18:59,633
You can do it, Angel and Calix!

350
00:18:59,767 --> 00:19:00,700
Go!

351
00:19:00,833 --> 00:19:01,867
Get set...

352
00:19:04,467 --> 00:19:05,333
Go!

353
00:19:05,467 --> 00:19:07,533
Go, Brighton Bay!

354
00:19:07,667 --> 00:19:17,633
[PEOPLE CHEERING]

355
00:19:19,267 --> 00:19:22,200
We have three teams vying...

356
00:19:26,767 --> 00:19:27,800
Oh, no!

357
00:19:33,233 --> 00:19:34,400
Unfortunately...

358
00:19:34,533 --> 00:19:38,133
the boat of Brighton Bay Academy
has collapsed.

359
00:19:38,433 --> 00:19:39,300
Oh, my goodness.

360
00:19:39,433 --> 00:19:41,133
- What?
- Brighton Bay lost.

361
00:19:41,267 --> 00:19:42,300
This can't be happening.

362
00:19:42,433 --> 00:19:44,433
We lost!

363
00:19:44,567 --> 00:19:46,300
Oh, my gosh.

364
00:19:46,433 --> 00:19:48,133
- It's Angel, Bro.
- It's Angel's fault.

365
00:19:48,267 --> 00:19:49,367
- Such a show-off.

366
00:19:49,500 --> 00:19:50,867
She always acts like she knows
everything.

367
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:52,000
So annoying.

368
00:19:52,133 --> 00:19:53,800
Angel!

369
00:19:53,933 --> 00:19:56,800
The previous front-runner,
Brighton Bay Academy,

370
00:19:56,933 --> 00:19:58,733
is eliminated
from the competition.

371
00:19:58,867 --> 00:19:59,967
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC]

372
00:20:00,100 --> 00:20:01,900
[PEOPLE CHEERING]

373
00:20:02,067 --> 00:20:05,400
Holy Crest!

374
00:20:05,533 --> 00:20:06,633
I told you we'd sink. See?

375
00:20:06,767 --> 00:20:09,067
We're the only team that sank.

376
00:20:09,200 --> 00:20:10,067
Fine.

377
00:20:10,200 --> 00:20:11,667
You're the expert.

378
00:20:11,800 --> 00:20:14,633
[STUDENTS SQUEALING]

379
00:20:14,767 --> 00:20:16,200
Students, students.

380
00:20:17,700 --> 00:20:18,767
Oh, my gosh.

381
00:20:21,600 --> 00:20:22,967
Just shut up, will you?

382
00:20:31,233 --> 00:20:33,667
Pacific! Pacific!

383
00:20:34,500 --> 00:20:35,733
Calix, don't walk away from me.

384
00:20:35,900 --> 00:20:37,500
I'm still talking to you.

385
00:20:40,400 --> 00:20:41,900
There's nothing I can do now.

386
00:20:42,033 --> 00:20:43,433
Okay?

387
00:20:43,567 --> 00:20:44,700
It's done.

388
00:20:44,833 --> 00:20:45,867
We lost.

389
00:20:47,333 --> 00:20:49,800
It's just a competition, Angel.

390
00:20:49,933 --> 00:20:50,967
Move on.

391
00:20:52,500 --> 00:20:54,333
You know what, stop crying.

392
00:20:54,467 --> 00:20:55,833
You're embarrassing yourself.

393
00:20:57,100 --> 00:20:59,033
Move on?

394
00:20:59,167 --> 00:21:01,500
Winning QuizCon meant
so much to me.

395
00:21:01,633 --> 00:21:04,067
It was incredibly important
to me, Calix.

396
00:21:05,233 --> 00:21:06,300
And why is that?

397
00:21:07,933 --> 00:21:09,567
Do you think I wanted
this to happen?

398
00:21:11,533 --> 00:21:13,267
I hate losing too, Angel.

399
00:21:15,500 --> 00:21:17,100
You know what,
this is all your fault.

400
00:21:18,133 --> 00:21:19,200
You should...

401
00:21:19,333 --> 00:21:21,000
never have been my partner.

402
00:21:22,867 --> 00:21:24,667
You just distracted me.

403
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:26,133
Distracted?

404
00:21:27,167 --> 00:21:29,000
You're the stubborn one.

405
00:21:29,133 --> 00:21:32,700
You're the know-it-all whose
actions caused our boat to sink.

406
00:21:34,400 --> 00:21:35,233
[SNIFFLES]

407
00:21:35,367 --> 00:21:37,700
You never take accountability
for anything.

408
00:21:39,067 --> 00:21:40,400
Accountability.

409
00:21:41,700 --> 00:21:44,000
What exactly do you want
to hear.

410
00:21:44,133 --> 00:21:45,467
You want me to apologize?

411
00:21:46,533 --> 00:21:48,000
Why would I say sorry?

412
00:21:50,167 --> 00:21:52,400
Do you think this isn't
humiliating for me too?

413
00:21:54,233 --> 00:21:55,800
What would people think of me?

414
00:21:55,933 --> 00:21:58,900
Well, that's the difference
between us, Calix.

415
00:21:59,267 --> 00:22:01,500
You fight for yourself
and your image.

416
00:22:01,633 --> 00:22:03,733
I fight for my grandfather.

417
00:22:03,867 --> 00:22:06,000
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

418
00:22:06,133 --> 00:22:07,467
That prize money,

419
00:22:09,200 --> 00:22:13,000
would've been a huge help with
my grandfather's hospital bills.

420
00:22:14,167 --> 00:22:17,333
I needed that prize money
for his procedure, Calix.

421
00:22:18,967 --> 00:22:21,233
That's why I agreed
to be your partner.

422
00:22:23,667 --> 00:22:25,433
You're really heartless.

423
00:22:26,867 --> 00:22:28,867
All you ever think about
is yourself.

424
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:33,933
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

425
00:22:38,667 --> 00:22:42,267
<i>Coming up tomorrow
on You're My Favorite Song...</i>

426
00:22:42,400 --> 00:22:45,733
I want to know who that girl
with them at the resort is,

427
00:22:45,867 --> 00:22:47,200
that Angel.

428
00:22:48,567 --> 00:22:50,600
I heard Beverly adopted her.

429
00:22:50,733 --> 00:22:53,233
Find out everything you can
about this girl

430
00:22:54,600 --> 00:22:56,900
because I'm going
to destroy her life.

431
00:22:57,933 --> 00:22:59,900
The kid is completely exhausted.

432
00:23:00,033 --> 00:23:03,367
They've been doing nonstop
local tours with Siklab.

433
00:23:03,500 --> 00:23:07,467
Your job is to make sure he
looks good in front of his fans!

434
00:23:07,600 --> 00:23:10,733
Siklab! Sik...
[AUDIENCE SCREAMING]

435
00:23:10,867 --> 00:23:12,267
[SHRIEKS]

436
00:23:12,400 --> 00:23:14,500
Miguel! Miguel!
